fix: reliability round — storage switch, launch watchers, links, secrets, a11y

Publishes the reviewed fixes from the working repository (code only; the local
planning docs stay out as usual). Everything below was re-verified inside this
release copy: npm test 84, npm run build, cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy
--workspace --all-targets -D warnings, cargo test --workspace 313 passed.

- storage: the data-root switch adopted the new path before the backend did
  (a refused root left the field and the disk disagreeing), cancelling a
  migration reported failure, and the first-run choice did not re-read the
  stores. The switch now goes through setRootVerified and reports a refusal.
- launch: adopted processes are watched for exit (they kept their entry and
  their WebUI window forever), the launch watcher only closes the window of
  its own pid, and kill_tree has a 10s deadline instead of hanging a stop.
- links: pnpm lays a plugin's dependencies out as junctions into the
  instance's own node_modules/.pnpm — measured on Windows — so a copy now
  carries links that live inside the copied tree (Preserve gained
  source_root/dest_root and callers pass the final path, not the staging
  name), and a migration translates them with the moving subtree.
- secrets: log tails are redacted before they reach the UI (dsh web prints the
  per-boot WebUI token on the first line), cordis.patch.yml is written
  tmp+rename, the manifest temp name is per-writer, and stop verifies the pid
  identity before killing.
- stores/UI: plugin toggles and API-config saves are serialized instead of
  dropping the user's edit, and a WebUI that could not open says so.
- a11y: measured contrast — ink-faint 2.72:1 → 4.60:1 light, 3.46:1 → 4.59:1
  dark, muted moved to 5.95:1; dialogs are labelled and trap/return focus;
  menus are keyboard-navigable; every switch has a name.

Windows CI path assertions (8.3 short names vs long names) are fixed by
comparing directory identity.